three things that nobody in the YouTube

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.480
space is talking about, and I call them

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.280
the flatline triggers. And once you see

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:26.160
them, you can't unsee them. And I know

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.120
that because I felt that same flatline

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.800
hundreds of times across five different

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.640
failed channels before I figured out

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.400
what was actually going on. And here's

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.240
the thing, the reason your videos stop

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.080
getting views has almost nothing to do

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.600
with the stuff most gurus are teaching.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.200
And I went from struggling to get views

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.560
on five different channels to building a

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.560
channel with over 1.5 million

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.680
subscribers that's generated millions of

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.520
dollars. And more importantly, I've

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.280
helped clients go from making zero from

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.000
YouTube or $1,000 a month up to over

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.360
$186,000

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.840
a month, and some even getting up to

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.560
$500,000 a month and eight figures a

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.560
year. So, let's get into the three

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.040
flatline triggers. Now, before I walk

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.920
you through each flatline trigger, you

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.879
need to understand something fundamental

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.000
about how YouTube actually works.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:08.960
YouTube is a testing machine. When you

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.560
upload a video, it shows it to a small

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.960
group of people first. Think of it like

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.680
a test audience. And YouTube is watching

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.120
everything. Whether people click,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.000
whether they actually watch, whether

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.880
they stick around or bounce in 10

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.880
seconds. And if those early signals are

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.160
good, people click, they watch, they

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.480
stay, YouTube goes, "Okay, this is

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:27.240
working." And they push it to more

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:29.600
people. But, if those early signals are

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.200
bad, YouTube goes, "All right, nobody

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.800
wants this." And they stop showing it.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.280
That's your flatline. That's the moment

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.240
that you refresh the analytics and

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.840
nothing's moving. Now, most creators see

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.320
the flatline happen and they think, "I

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.960
need to fix my SEO. I need better tags.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.480
I need to optimize my description." And

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.640
they go down this rabbit hole of

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:47.400
optimization hacks that for most of you

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:49.080
don't matter nearly as much as the gurus

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.880
want you to believe. And I get it, it

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.520
feels productive to spend an hour

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.440
tweaking your tags and renaming your

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.480
file, and it feels like you're doing

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
something. You feel like a spy that

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.880
figured something out that nobody else

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.160
knows. You know the secret. But it's the

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.720
equivalent of rearranging deck chairs on

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:07.120
the Titanic. You're polishing the 5%

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.399
while the 95% is broken. And a lot of

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.080
YouTube gurus teaching that stuff

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:11.480
haven't actually built real businesses

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.840
on the platform. They're just teaching

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.080
YouTube theory, not YouTube practice.

