each of these flatline triggers, what

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:29.080
they are, why they kill your videos, and

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.560
exactly how to fix each one. Let's start

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.880
with the deadliest one. The first

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.480
flatline trigger is what I call a ghost

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.440
launch. A ghost launch is when you

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.920
upload a video into a market where

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.160
there's no proven demand. You're

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.040
essentially launching to ghosts. Nobody

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:43.680
asked for this video, nobody's searching

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.120
for it, nobody is hungry for this

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.760
information right now. You pressed

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.000
publish and the video entered a void.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.600
And this is by far the number one reason

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.520
that videos die, and it's the one that

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.240
nobody wants to hear. Because it means

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.120
the problem isn't your editing, it's not

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.920
your camera, it's not your charisma. The

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.160
problem is the idea of your video. The

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.040
video idea is the single most important

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.800
factor in whether your video succeeds or

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:06.280
fails. It's more important than anything

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.000
else. Let me show you the actual

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.720
hierarchy. So, here's the analogy that

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.920
will make this click. You open the best

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.600
pizza restaurant in the world,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.960
incredible pizza, perfect service,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.160
beautiful branding. But you put it in

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.160
the middle of a desert where there's

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.600
nobody around for 50 miles. You're going

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.280
to fail. Not because your product is

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.280
bad, but because there's no one to buy

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.040
your stuff. There's no starving crowd of

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:26.240
people. Now, flip it. You open a

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.360
mediocre hot dog stand right outside of

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.240
a college bar at 1:00 a.m. when all the

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.240
drunk kids are pouring out starving.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:34.000
