00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:37.480
flatline trigger is what I call the

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:39.080
broken chain. And here's what I mean. On

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:41.120
YouTube, there's a chain of trust

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:43.360
between you and the viewer, and it has

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:45.560
exactly three links, the thumbnail, the

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:47.600
title, and the intro. Each link has one

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:49.520
job, hand the viewer off to the next

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.320
link. And the thumbnail's job is to stop

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:52.920
the scroll and get the eyeball. The

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:55.000
title's job is to earn the click, and

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:57.280
the intro's job is to earn the watch.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.800
And when this chain link is intact, when

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.800
all three links are connected and

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:03.160
telling the same story, viewers flow

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:05.120
seamlessly from seeing your video to

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:07.440
actually watching it. But when even one

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:09.320
link breaks, the whole chain snaps, and

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:11.160
your video flatlines. So, here's how the

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:13.120
chain usually breaks. Break number one,

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:14.800
the thumbnail and the title say the same

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.600
thing. They use the same words, the same

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.280
numbers, and the same message. That's

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.440
redundant. Your thumbnail should be more

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:22.720
emotional and visual. I'd say about 90%

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:24.640
emotional, 10% analytical. Your title

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:26.800
should be a bit more balanced, 50%

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:28.080
emotional, 50% analytical, with

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:29.560
searchable keywords close to the

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:31.680
beginning. And most importantly, they

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:33.280
should complement each other, not repeat

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.360
each other. And a good rule here is put

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.039
numbers in the thumbnail, put dates and

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:38.840
keywords in the title. And let's be

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:40.200
honest, if you're going to clickbait a

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:42.000
little bit, do it in the thumbnail

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.120
because viewers can't see it anymore

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.880
once they click. And that's just the

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:46.280
reality of how YouTube works, and most

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.080
of the top YouTubers do that a little

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:50.040
bit. But the title stays visible the

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.000
whole time they're watching, so keep it

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.960
honest. Break number two, the intro

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:56.440
doesn't deliver on the promise. Your

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:58.000
thumbnail has a shocked face, your title

